FEATURE: modal-displayer-verification
DATE: 2026-08-03
SCOPE: verify the ModalDisplayer module, optimise where needed, and document it

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) — the only project affected. No other project in the
workspace consumes these files. There is no build step, no package manifest and no
dependency graph to propagate through: the library is shipped as source and loaded
directly by consuming pages, so all changes take effect on the next page load.

Consumer-visible surface:
  - vUX-modalDisplayer.js       behaviour fixes; no public API added or removed
  - assets/css/modalDisplayer.css  one new rule (.vModal.xScroll)

No public API was renamed, removed or added, so no entry is required in
ChangeLog.md's rename record and no version bump is implied. Existing consumer code
continues to work unchanged; the fixes only make documented behaviour that was
previously broken actually take effect.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION METHOD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The repository has no test runner, so the module was verified by driving a real
browser (headless Chromium via Playwright) against a new example page served over
HTTP from the repository root, asserting DOM state, computed styles, callback
invocation and scroll position across the full open/close cycle of every effect.

Baseline run before any fix:   23 passed, 6 failed
Final run after fixes:         32 passed, 0 failed

The test harness itself lives outside the repository (it is a verification tool,
not a shipped artifact); the example page it drives is committed under
examples/modal/ as documentation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEFECTS FOUND AND FIXED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. ReferenceError on tall modals (crash)
   positionVertically() called `VerticalScroll.query(...)`. VerticalScroll is
   defined nowhere in the library. Any modal within 100px of the viewport height
   threw, aborting the open half-way and corrupting state so the following close()
   also threw. Tall modals were entirely unusable. The surrounding branches were
   found to be redundant (both live branches applied identical styles; the third was
   unreachable), so the function was reduced to its single meaningful behaviour.

2. Tall modals unreachable below the fold
   The overlay carried the class `xScroll`, which no stylesheet defined. With the
   body frozen at `position: fixed` and the overlay at `overflow: visible`, nothing
   could scroll, so content past the first viewport height was unreachable. Added
   `.vModal.xScroll { overflow-y: auto; overflow-x: hidden }`.

3. config.overlayStyle had no effect
   `overlay["style"] = overlayStyle` assigns to a read-only CSSStyleDeclaration and
   was silently discarded; the overlay was always transparent. Now applied as the
   `background` declaration.

4. Duplicate overlay with a second instance
   The dedupe guard queried `style[data-id='vModalStyles']`, but the marker is on
   the overlay div, so it never matched. A second ModalDisplayer appended a second
   overlay and the module's `$$.ss(".vModal")` lookups then resolved ambiguously,
   breaking both instances. Selector corrected to `div[data-id=...]`.

5. openProcessor never fired for the default effect
   The callback was only invoked from the transitionend handler, which effect
   "none" (the default) never reaches. Now called directly in the none path.

6. Per-trigger widths leaked permanently
   A trigger carrying the widths attribute overwrote modalWidths with no reset, so
   its sizing applied to every modal opened afterwards. Defaults are now restored
   when a trigger omits the attribute.

7. Blur overlay never removed on the "none" close path
   With overlayBackgroundType = "blur" and the default effect, the vxKit blur class
   was added on open but never removed, leaving the host page permanently blurred.

8. Host page scroll-behavior permanently rewritten
   Closing a modal set an inline `scroll-behavior: smooth` on <html> and never
   reverted it, silently changing every subsequent scroll on the consumer's site.
   Now suppressed only for the duration of the restore jump, then restored.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPTIMISATIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- getDimensionOfHidden() was called twice per open to read two members of the same
  result. That helper mutates element styles and reads scrollHeight/scrollWidth,
  forcing synchronous layout each time. Now called once.
- Removed an unused `$$.ss("html").scrollHeight` read from initialize(), another
  forced layout serving nothing.
- Removed ten dead closure variables (totalHeight, closeButton, sX, endSy,
  scrollable, modalHeigthBelow, modalHeigthAbove, paddingTop and related), all
  leftovers of the pre-v4 positioning workflow.
- Trigger and close-button matching now uses closest() instead of
  classList.contains(), so triggers containing nested markup (icons, spans) work.
  This is a usability fix as much as a cleanup.

Net effect on vUX-modalDisplayer.js: 69 lines changed, 39 removed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DOCUMENTATION ADDED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- doc/modal-displayer.md — full usage guide: trigger-driven model, quick start,
  complete config table with types and defaults, API, effects, tall-modal
  behaviour, and the constraints that are easy to get wrong.
- examples/modal/ — runnable demo (page, wiring module, README) covering all four
  effects, per-trigger widths, a tall scrolling modal, all three close routes and
  the open/close callbacks.
- doc/README.md — guide registered in the index; example linked.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIRMED WORKING (unchanged behaviour)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All four effects open and close cleanly; content is restored to its original
position and hidden state after every cycle; body scroll locking and scroll
position restoration; close by close button, Escape key and overlay click;
exitOnAway; reopening after close; live width recalculation on browser resize;
the mainForm and displayForm getters; and automatic linking of
assets/css/modalDisplayer.css through the assetPath contract.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KNOWN LIMITATIONS (documented, not fixed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- Only one modal may be open at a time; the module keeps a single overlay and a
  single set of state variables. Stacked modals would require a redesign.
- Modal content is cloned via innerHTML into the overlay, so event listeners bound
  directly to nodes inside the content do not survive an open/close cycle. The
  guide directs consumers to delegate, or to bind through displayForm on open.
